[[:db/retract 17592186117517 :answer-field/choices 17592186117520] [:db/retract 17592186117517 :answer-field/choices 17592186117521] [:db/retract 17592186117517 :answer-field/choices 17592186117522] [:db/retract 17592186117517 :answer-field/choices 17592186117519] {:db/id 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a985335b-cba4-5e25-b462-ecfeb2395155" "question-8e5d0c94-6cbf-5053-b8da-ce1333f1257b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119652 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](images/64/64a3661b0699fbde542ed1709bacf569f681477a5f824f0650b07d9060b82dae.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4y+6z+25 & =0 \\\\ 3(3-4t)+4(-1+2t)+6(2+3t)+25 & =0 \\\\ 9-12t-4+8t+12+18t+25 & =0 \\\\ 14t & =-42 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4(-3)=15 \\\\ y=-1+2(-3)=-7 \\\\ z=2+3(-3)=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2968eff5-6f3b-5cf4-97d0-686663582eb3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a985335b-cba4-5e25-b462-ecfeb2395155" :question/id #uuid "a985335b-cba4-5e25-b462-ecfeb2395155" :question/math-academy-id "q-108315" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,-3,4⟩+t⟨4,-2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩=1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩ & =1 \\\\ ⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩ & =1 \\\\ -2(1+4t)+(-3)(-3-2t)+2\\cdot (4+t) & =1 \\\\ -2-8t+9+6t+8+2t & =1 \\\\ 15 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3a04dab5-4de0-5a23-bb85-4c890b9f023c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3a04dab5-4de0-5a23-bb85-4c890b9f023c" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a04dab5-4de0-5a23-bb85-4c890b9f023c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-25dfd479-4874-55fc-ac79-5aafbe7a30f4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-00128b0b-75f1-5ff4-8a3e-54c15cf052dd" "answer-0db1cb8d-ae91-58aa-ba6d-996ec7b29ea2" "answer-66855eaf-d25e-59dd-8568-e9296afde634" "answer-bc96ece3-ea6d-5cb5-94a3-9ae65aed87a5" "answer-25dfd479-4874-55fc-ac79-5aafbe7a30f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00128b0b-75f1-5ff4-8a3e-54c15cf052dd" :answer/id #uuid "00128b0b-75f1-5ff4-8a3e-54c15cf052dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-3,-1,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0db1cb8d-ae91-58aa-ba6d-996ec7b29ea2" :answer/id #uuid "0db1cb8d-ae91-58aa-ba6d-996ec7b29ea2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-7,1,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66855eaf-d25e-59dd-8568-e9296afde634" :answer/id #uuid "66855eaf-d25e-59dd-8568-e9296afde634" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,-3,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc96ece3-ea6d-5cb5-94a3-9ae65aed87a5" :answer/id #uuid "bc96ece3-ea6d-5cb5-94a3-9ae65aed87a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,-5,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25dfd479-4874-55fc-ac79-5aafbe7a30f4" :answer/id #uuid "25dfd479-4874-55fc-ac79-5aafbe7a30f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120226 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩=4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+2t,2t,1+t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+2t,2t,1+t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =4 \\\\ ⟨3+2t,2t,1+t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =4 \\\\ 2(3+2t)-2t+4(1+t) & =4 \\\\ 6+4t-2t+4+4t & =4 \\\\ 6t & =-6 \\\\ t & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+2(-1),2(-1),1+(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(1,-2,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186117517 :answer-field/correct "answer-266afbbe-3a5e-5405-b0ca-02646080f267" :answer-field/choices ["answer-266afbbe-3a5e-5405-b0ca-02646080f267" "answer-c7bcd1a1-4127-5759-8dbc-c749468c35cb" "answer-cfddec79-fecc-5697-9dc1-640959c5e5fc" "answer-676389da-d8bf-5b92-bcd7-a398a98b3965"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-266afbbe-3a5e-5405-b0ca-02646080f267" :answer/id #uuid "266afbbe-3a5e-5405-b0ca-02646080f267" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,-2,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7bcd1a1-4127-5759-8dbc-c749468c35cb" :answer/id #uuid "c7bcd1a1-4127-5759-8dbc-c749468c35cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,-1,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfddec79-fecc-5697-9dc1-640959c5e5fc" :answer/id #uuid "cfddec79-fecc-5697-9dc1-640959c5e5fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,0,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-676389da-d8bf-5b92-bcd7-a398a98b3965" :answer/id #uuid "676389da-d8bf-5b92-bcd7-a398a98b3965" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(7,4,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8e5d0c94-6cbf-5053-b8da-ce1333f1257b" :question/id #uuid "8e5d0c94-6cbf-5053-b8da-ce1333f1257b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108308" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-1,2,1⟩+t⟨3,0,2⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=13.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =13 \\\\ ⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =13 \\\\ 1(-1+3t)-2+2(1+2t) & =13 \\\\ -1+3t-2+2+4t & =13 \\\\ 7t & =14 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-1+3(2),2,1+2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,2,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,2,5).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c7e90ddb-8e9f-5cb4-bec1-a99d63f38772"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c7e90ddb-8e9f-5cb4-bec1-a99d63f38772" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7e90ddb-8e9f-5cb4-bec1-a99d63f38772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8834e13a-22fa-5aac-a999-328918db52aa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa261700-7670-52be-9dc1-2ffc7832aa15" "answer-f64b86a2-04c6-5e9a-9cf2-346fe66c641a" "answer-b83d1b54-86e9-5e63-af2b-8d6d7fdb32d1" "answer-8834e13a-22fa-5aac-a999-328918db52aa" "answer-96d49a2f-474b-5bba-b6c4-17e8726cbd43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa261700-7670-52be-9dc1-2ffc7832aa15" :answer/id #uuid "fa261700-7670-52be-9dc1-2ffc7832aa15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-4,2,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f64b86a2-04c6-5e9a-9cf2-346fe66c641a" :answer/id #uuid "f64b86a2-04c6-5e9a-9cf2-346fe66c641a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-7,2,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b83d1b54-86e9-5e63-af2b-8d6d7fdb32d1" :answer/id #uuid "b83d1b54-86e9-5e63-af2b-8d6d7fdb32d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,2,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8834e13a-22fa-5aac-a999-328918db52aa" :answer/id #uuid "8834e13a-22fa-5aac-a999-328918db52aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,2,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96d49a2f-474b-5bba-b6c4-17e8726cbd43" :answer/id #uuid "96d49a2f-474b-5bba-b6c4-17e8726cbd43" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186399629 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2t \\\\ y=-3+4t \\\\ z=5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+2y-z=33.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y-z & =33 \\\\ 3(4+2t)+2(-3+4t)-(5t) & =33 \\\\ 12+6t-6+8t-5t & =33 \\\\ 9t & =27 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2(3)=10 \\\\ y=-3+4(3)=9 \\\\ z=5(3)=15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(10,9,15).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186244121 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:x-3y+2z=12.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y+2z & =12 \\\\ 1(7+2t)-3(3+t)+2(1-t) & =12 \\\\ 7+2t-9-3t+2-2t & =12 \\\\ -3t & =12 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=7+2(-4)=-1 \\\\ y=3+(-4)=-1 \\\\ z=1-(-4)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-1,-1,5).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186244122 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=-3+t \\\\ z=4+2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+y-4z+45=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y-4z+45 & =0 \\\\ 3(2-3t)+(-3+t)-4(4+2t) & =-45 \\\\ 6-9t-3+t-16-8t & =-45 \\\\ -16t & =-32 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3(2)=-4 \\\\ y=-3+2=-1 \\\\ z=4+2(2)=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-4,-1,8).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186244124 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3t \\\\ y=5+2t \\\\ z=-7+t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+3y+5z-11=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+5z-11 & =0 \\\\ 4(9-3t)+3(5+2t)+5(-7+t) & =11 \\\\ 36-12t+15+6t-35+5t & =11 \\\\ -t & =-5 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3(5)=-6 \\\\ y=5+2(5)=15 \\\\ z=-7+5=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-6,15,-2).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186342128 :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-t \\\\ y=4+2t \\\\ z=-6-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+6y-3z-130=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+6y-3z-130 & =0 \\\\ 4(5-t)+6(4+2t)-3(-6-3t) & =130 \\\\ 20-4t+24+12t+18+9t & =130 \\\\ 17t & =68 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=5-4=1 \\\\ y=4+2(4)=12 \\\\ z=-6-3(4)=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(1,12,-18).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-2968eff5-6f3b-5cf4-97d0-686663582eb3" :question/id #uuid "2968eff5-6f3b-5cf4-97d0-686663582eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-108369" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-2,1,4⟩+t⟨3,2,-6⟩,\\,Π:-4x+3y-z-11=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x+3y-z-11 & =0 \\\\ -4x+3y-z & =11 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ -4(-2+3t)+3(1+2t)-(4-6t) & =11 \\\\ 8-12t+3+6t-4+6t & =11 \\\\ 7 & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-817f92e5-c306-5bc0-98bb-5216ce23f4dd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-817f92e5-c306-5bc0-98bb-5216ce23f4dd" :answer-field/id #uuid "817f92e5-c306-5bc0-98bb-5216ce23f4dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f85e9e92-164c-5dbe-a1e2-300ee4897290" :answer-field/choices ["answer-613bfe5f-02e2-5735-9f79-164b162ce348" "answer-a6b4a532-3b78-5ed1-a6e7-746b7ec7ab3f" "answer-d748dd3f-d487-5117-bef8-07f995fa3631" "answer-de970a68-1f18-57df-a82c-3fb7858ebc0a" "answer-f85e9e92-164c-5dbe-a1e2-300ee4897290"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-613bfe5f-02e2-5735-9f79-164b162ce348" :answer/id #uuid "613bfe5f-02e2-5735-9f79-164b162ce348" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-5,-1,10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6b4a532-3b78-5ed1-a6e7-746b7ec7ab3f" :answer/id #uuid "a6b4a532-3b78-5ed1-a6e7-746b7ec7ab3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-8,-3,16)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d748dd3f-d487-5117-bef8-07f995fa3631" :answer/id #uuid "d748dd3f-d487-5117-bef8-07f995fa3631" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,3,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de970a68-1f18-57df-a82c-3fb7858ebc0a" :answer/id #uuid "de970a68-1f18-57df-a82c-3fb7858ebc0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,5,-8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f85e9e92-164c-5dbe-a1e2-300ee4897290" :answer/id #uuid "f85e9e92-164c-5dbe-a1e2-300ee4897290" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120019 :activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
